SUMMARY:HTC 101: The Beginner’s Guide to Historic Tax Credits
DTSTAMP:20260810T100443Z
DTSTART:20260820T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:Each historic tax credit (HTC) rehabilitation project is unique
	 and has inherent challenges. Learn how to anticipate if a rehabilitation 
	is feasible. Our presentation will consider how to analyze\, evaluate\, an
	d apply HTC principles in real-world projects through examples\, while und
	erstanding the collaboration required between preservation professionals\,
	 architects\, and developers to achieve both regulatory compliance and fin
	ancial success. Examples will be pulled from several projects in Texas. \n
	Presented by: William R. Franks Consulting and Ryan Historic Advisors \nHo
	sted by: AIAH Historic Resources Committee \nAIA Credit: 1.0 LU \nSchedule
	:  \n\n5:30pm Social\n6:00pm – 7:00pm Presentation\n\n  \n  \n \n\nhttps:/
	/architecturehouston.org/event/htc-101-the-beginners-guide-to-historic-tax
	-credits/\n\nFrom AIA Houston
URL:https://architecturehouston.org/event/htc-101-the-beginners-guide-to-hi
	storic-tax-credits/
LOCATION:Architecture Center Houston\, 902 Commerce St.\, Houston\, TX\, 77
	002\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:aia-houston
CATEGORIES:AIA Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
